	(text "MJ-14 FIXED - line UV sense fitted (clamped network, InnoSwitch3-AQ datasheet Fig. 15).\nR616-R619 4x 300k (RU = 1.20 M) + R630 210k (RL) + D620 9.1 V zener at the RL top node.\nBrown-in V_UV+ = I_UV+ x (RU+RL) + 1.37 V; I_UV+ 22.1/26.1/30.4 uA over temp ->\n32.5 / 38.2 / 44.2 V.  Max 44.2 V < the 48 V SPEC 11.1 minimum line: starts at 48 V.\nBrown-out (I_UV- 19.7-27 uA) = 29.2-39.4 V.  D620 clamps node X at 9.1 V so the V-pin\ncurrent saturates at (9.1-1.37)/210k = 36.8 uA, far below I_OV+ min 98 uA - the OV /\nremote-disable function therefore never trips over the 48-500 V range (the fixed 4.4:1\nI_OV+/I_UV+ ratio could not otherwise span 9.4:1).  D620 dissipation 3.4 mW at 500 V.\nDatasheet has no closed-form formula for the unclamped case - CONFIRM WITH PI PIXls [TBV].\nWithout this network DER-948Q 4.2 warns regulation fails at high load below 80 VDC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.66 95.25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d2487c2a-d317-446f-a651-5b8a9960dbb9")
	)
	(text "CR-4 FIXED - RCD clamp respec.  R603/R604/R612-R615 = 6x 39k 1206 (0.5 W, 200 V working,\nROHM ESR18 class) wired 3 series x 2 parallel = 58.5 k.  Old build was 2x 390k 0603 in\nparallel (195 k) on parts rated 75 V / 0.1 W - 3-5x over voltage and over power.\nV_OR = 15.5 V x 12.5 = 194 V.  P_leak = 0.5 x Lk x I_LIM^2 x f (f 55.5 kHz, I_LIM 2.30 A\ntyp standard setting) and V_clamp solves V(V-194)/58500 = P_leak:\n   Lk = 1.0 uH -> V_clamp 231 V -> V_DS 681 V @450 V bus / 731 V @500 V\n   Lk = 2.0 uH -> V_clamp 261 V -> V_DS 711 V / 761 V\n   Lk = 4.0 uH -> V_clamp 306 V -> V_DS 756 V / 806 V\n   Lk = 6.5 uH -> V_clamp 352 V -> V_DS 802 V / 852 V   (6.5 uH = DER-948Q T1 spec limit)\nPer-part stress worst case 0.35 W and 117 V - inside the 1206 ratings in every case.\n*** OPEN: T601 LEAKAGE INDUCTANCE MUST BE MEASURED ON THE FIRST WOUND SAMPLE. ***\nPI keeps continuous drain below 725 V; that requires Lk <= 2.0 uH, which must therefore\nbe written into the T601 purchase spec (DER-948Q allows 6.5 uH - not good enough here).\nBVDSS 900 V is respected in all four cases, but only just at 6.5 uH.\nD601 also sees the full V_DS: US1M is 1000 V, 80% at 806 V.  DER-948Q uses TWO 1000 V\ndiodes in series to stay under 70% - REVIEW ITEM, not changed here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 128 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "baa6340b-b4f4-40f3-8933-b8ecb4260949")
	)
	(text "CR-5 FIXED - core saturation at the current limit.  C606 (BPP) 4.7 uF -> 0.47 uF, which\nselects the STANDARD I_LIMIT instead of I_LIMIT+1.  Controller stays INN3990CQ.\nB_pk = Lp x I_LIM / (Np x Ae) = 422.6 uH x I / (25 x 108 mm^2) = 0.1565 T/A:\n   was 4.7 uF -> I_LIMIT+1 2.576 A typ / 2.886 A worst -> 403 mT / 452 mT\n   now 0.47 uF -> I_LIMIT   2.300 A typ / 2.576 A worst -> 360 mT / 403 mT\nDER-948Q designs its identical T1 to B_PEAK 376 mT, so the typical case is now BELOW\nPI's own reference point.  3C96 saturates at ~410-440 mT at 100 C.\nDatasheet has only two BPP settings (0.47 uF and 4.7 uF) - there is no reduced setting\nin the -AQ family.  This also keeps more output-power headroom than swapping to\nINN3999CQ would (2.30 A vs 2.13 A), so no controller change and no pinout re-check.\nC607 100 nF stays in parallel with C606 (open-BPP protection, datasheet recommendation).\nRESIDUAL: worst-case 403 mT leaves only ~2-7% margin.  If the wound sample measures\nhigh, respec Np 25T -> 27T with the gap re-cut for the same Lp (B falls to 333/373 mT)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130 130 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c03d4e74-cf52-46f4-bf4b-4fde43c81891")
	)
	(text "MJ-19 - aux input priority (D020) now actually implemented by setpoint offset:\nflyback 14.97 V (R609/R610 143k/13.2k @ 1.265 V) vs LM5175 16.45 V (R623 88.7k -> 97.6k).\nWorst case: LM5175 min 16.45 x 0.975 = 16.04 V > flyback max 14.97 x 1.03 = 15.42 V,\nmargin 0.62 V - the aux unit always holds the rail and the flyback idles.  Previously the\ntwo bands overlapped (15.02 V vs 14.97 V) so whichever ran high won at random.\nMN-7 also resolved: 12 V rail duty headroom improves on the aux rail.  Everything on\nAUX_15V must tolerate 16.9 V worst case - checked: C609/C610 25 V, C640/C645 50 V,\nLMR33630 36 V, Q605/U604 fine."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.66 108 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7bd5c6cd-9797-4026-a765-c7e4f604e8e5")
	)
	(text "INSULATION CAVEAT (D017) - the four gate-drive transformers T602-T605 (WE 750316856)\ncarry SUPPLEMENTARY / FUNCTIONAL insulation only, 600 Vrms working; their 2.5 kV AC\nfigure is a type-test hipot, not a reinforced certification.  The REINFORCED barrier on\nthe gate-drive path therefore rests ENTIRELY on the 1ED3491 driver ICs (SPEC 5).\nThis remains OPEN against SPEC 10 until the compliance target (SPEC 14 item 4) is fixed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 281.94 300 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "620a947c-2ba3-4ab5-8eea-711095219487")
	)

