	(text "D026 - +15 V GATE RAIL POST-REGULATION.  REQUIRED: the raw rail alone breaks the module AMR.\nRaw secondary = 5 V +-2.5% x 4.67 = 22.77-23.93 V per half, less the SS310 Vf; at light load the\n  leakage peak-charges the reservoir to ~24.9 V.  Minus the COM zener that is V_GS(on) = 20.3 V\n  against the FS02MR12A8MA2B +19 V ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM - a continuous overstress on all six switches.\n  A zener swap alone does NOT fix it; the +15 V leg has to be post-regulated.  (D607/D610/D613/D616\n  BZX384-C5V1 = 5.1 V +-5% -> 5.36 V also broke the -5 V static AMR: replaced, see below.)\nEach domain: R64x 470R from VGD_x_RAW feeds D62x (MMSZ5245C-E3-08, 15 V +-2%, 14.70-15.30 V at\n  I_ZT 8.5 mA, Z_ZT 16 R, 500 mW) in series with D62x (1N4148W-7-F, V_BE compensation) into the base\n  of Q60x (BCP56-16T1G, SOT-223, 80 V / 1 A, hFE 100-250) wired as an emitter follower to VGD_x_P.\n  V_GS(on) = Vz + Vf(diode) - V_BE(Q); the diode cancels V_BE and its tempco, leaving Vz +-0.15 V.\nWORST-CASE ARITHMETIC\n  V_GS(on) at 25 C   : 14.60 - 15.45 V  (module recommendation 15 V +-5% = 14.25 - 15.75 V)\n  V_GS(on) 0 to +70 C: 14.2 - 16.2 V.   Max term by term: 15.30 (Vz max) + 0.03 (Z_ZT x 1.9 mA over\n     I_ZT) + 0.68 (+13.5 mV/K x 50 K) + 0.755 (Vf hot) - 0.60 (V_BE hot) = 16.17 V.\n     *** 16.2 V vs the +19 V AMR = 2.8 V MARGIN.  Was 20.3 V, i.e. 1.3 V OVER. ***\n  V_GS(off) static   : D607/D610/D613/D616 now MM3Z4V7ST1G (4.55-4.75 V at I_ZT 5 mA, 80 R, 300 mW,\n     SOD-323).  Bias is the 6.0 mA split-zener preload R317/R327/R337/R347 on gate_drive - do NOT\n     duplicate it here.  4.75 + 1 mA x 80 R = 4.83 V, +0.2 mV/K x 45 K = 4.84 V at 70 C.\n     *** 4.84 V vs the -5 V static AMR = 0.16 V MARGIN.  Was up to 5.36 V. ***\n     RESIDUAL: the tempco limit is -3.5 mV/K, so at -40 C a worst-case part reaches 5.06 V.  SPEC\n     11.5 fixes only the +70 C internal maximum and no cold minimum; if -40 C is ever required,\n     substitute a 4.3 V part (the swing then becomes 15/-4.3 = 19.3 V, still inside every rating).\n  Zener bias current 0.9 - 10.4 mA over the 5 V-rail and load range; R64x dissipates 51 mW max.\nPASS-DEVICE THERMALS - V_CE x domain current, domain current = Qg x f_sw + driver Iq + 6 mA preload:\n  HS1/HS2/HS3   41 mA  (1.19 uC x 25 kHz = 29.8 mA, one switch each)   -> 0.15 W\n  LS           110 mA  (THREE drivers U304/U305/U306 share this rail)  -> 0.48 W\n  *** Q609 REQUIRES ITS SOT-223 COLLECTOR TAB ON >= 600 mm2 OF COPPER.  At the datasheet 83 C/W\n  that is Tj = 110 C at the 70 C internal ambient (SPEC 11.5); a bare land pattern (~200 C/W)\n  would exceed 150 C.  Q606-Q608 at 0.15 W are fine on minimum copper. ***\n  Also unverified and pre-existing: T605/U612 must carry 110 mA x ~20 V = 2.2 W on the LS domain.\nLAYOUT - THE FOUR BLOCKS ARE DRAWN TOGETHER BUT MUST NOT BE PLACED TOGETHER.  Each one belongs
  ENTIRELY INSIDE ITS OWN ISOLATED DOMAIN, beside T602/T603/T604/T605 respectively: for HS1-HS3
  VGD_x_RAW / _COM / _N float at the phase-node potential (up to 450 V + transient).  Keep the
  SPEC 10 barrier - no copper, silk or plane crossing between domains, and none of these parts
  on the control-ground side.  D629/Q610/D630/R648 belong at the J1203 aux input instead.
SOURCING: BZX384-B4V7,115 and every BZX384-B15 variant are at ZERO stock (DigiKey, 30-week lead);\n  the parts fitted are the stocked equivalents.  C662/C663 (and the equivalents in the other three\n  domains) are now the RAW-side reservoir; C684-C687 are the regulated-output bulk."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 420.37 27.94 0)
