			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "514e381f-7bf0-5c75-b6a6-3eff76bfac09")
	)
	(text "MN-14 FIXED - AUX INPUT PROTECTION (12-24 V feed, J1203 on the comms sheet).\nPreviously a reversed connection ran straight through the LM5175 body diodes with nothing in the way.\nD629 SMCJ36CA - BIDIRECTIONAL TVS, DO-214AB.  Littelfuse SMCJ datasheet: V_RWM 36 V, V_C 58.1 V at rated I_PP\n  at I_T 1 mA, 1500 W bidirectional.  36 V standoff is chosen so\n  a 24 V system's 36 V / 60 s jump start does NOT drive it into breakdown - a 26-30 V part would\n  conduct for the whole minute.  BIDIRECTIONAL rather than the unidirectional SMCJ40A because there\n  is no fuse on this input: reversed, the uni part forward-conducts and shorts the supply.  V_C is\n  identical for both, so the reverse blocking is free.\n  WHY 36 V NOT 40 V: SMCJ40CA clamps at 64.5 V, ABOVE the LM5175 60 V AMR and the DMP6023LE 60 V V_DSS -\n  a TVS that clamps above the parts it protects is decorative.  SMCJ36CA (V_C 58.1 V) clamps inside\n  both.  Its standoff sits at the 36 V jump-start level where leakage is uA-class for 60 s -
  the right trade.  An input fuse is still recommended and is NOT fitted.\nQ610 DMP6023LE-13 - P-FET reverse polarity (SOT-223, -60 V, 28 mR at V_GS -10 V, -7 A, 60 C/W).\n  DRAIN to the connector and SOURCE to the load, so the body diode blocks on a reversed input.\n  0.25 W at 3 A against 2.25 W for a Schottky, and it does not spend 0.75 V of the 12 V minimum\n  where the buck-boost still has to make 15 V.\nMANDATORY GATE CLAMP - V_GS(max) is +-20 V and in this topology the full input appears gate-to-\n  source, so 24 V nominal (let alone a 36 V jump start) destroys an unclamped gate.  R648 100k in\n  series with D630 MMSZ5243BT1G (13 V, SOD-123) across G-S: clamps at ~13-14 V, more than 5 V below\n  the 20 V limit and still well past the -10 V R_DS(on) test point.  A 15 V clamp was rejected -\n  15.75 V max plus tempco reaches ~17 V, only 14% below the limit.\nNOT A LOAD-DUMP DESIGN: ISO 7637-2 pulse 5a/5b is tens of joules against roughly 1 J of capability\n  here.  If an automotive compliance target is adopted, a load-dump-rated TVS or an active clamp\n  plus an input fuse are required.  AUX_IN is the connector-side net; AUX_IN_P is downstream of Q610."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
